        "And the height up the wall — that's what we need to find. Call it b.",
        "Now look at the shape these three lines have made. It's a right triangle. Pythagoras applies here directly.",
        "Apply the theorem: a squared plus b squared equals c squared. That means 5 squared plus b squared equals 13 squared.",
        "Now simplify: 25 plus b squared equals 169. So b squared equals 169 minus 25, which equals 144.",
        "Take the square root: b equals the square root of 144, which is 12.",
        "So the ladder reaches 12 feet up the wall. Beautifully simple — and this is exactly what real painters, electricians, and firefighters calculate daily."
